1554,100.34247,"China Street Ghaut","","","","","r","This colonial building houses the Penang branch of the Royal Malaysian Customs. It was completed in 1907 as a Malayan Railway station. As it is not beside a rail track, it was known as the only rail station in the world without a railway."],["Beach Street","sight",5.41827,100.34314,"","","","","","r","As the main Central Business District (CBD) of George Town, Beach Street is lined with mercantile buildings constructed between the 1880s and the 1950s. Among the landmarks along the street are the Standard Chartered Building, HSBC…"],["Wisma Yeap Chor Ee","sight",5.4153,100.34229,"China Street Ghaut","","","","","r","An elegant colonial building built in the 1920s, it once belonged to Yeap Chor Ee, a China-born tycoon. The building now houses @CAT, a coworking space popular amongst startups and freelancers."],["Made in Penang Interactive Museum","sight",5.41635,100.3436,"3 Weld Quay","Daily 10AM-6:30PM","","","","r","Housed within the Behn-Meyer Building which was built in the late 19th century, this interactive museum features various three-dimensional interactive art pieces that depict Penang's culture, history and lifestyle."],["Chinese Clan Jetties","sight",5.41258,100.34007,"Weld Quay","","","","","r","There are six clan jetties along the eastern coastline of George Town. They are worth walking to and looking at, as they provide an insight to the way local Chinese live in traditional huts built on the sea on stilts. Chew Jetty is the…"],["Occupy Beach Street","activity",5.41791,100.34276,"Beach Street","Sun 7AM-1PM","","","","r","Every Sunday morning, Beach Street, Bishop Street, Church Street and Church Street Ghaut are turned into car-free zones. Family-friendly recreational activities and roadside stalls will be set up along these roads."],["Woodlands Vegetarian Restaurant","restaurant",5.41796,100.34055,"60, Lebuh Penang","8:30AM-9PM","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"]]}